          <change when="2024-11-24T07:38:37-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Finalized - done</change>
          <change when="2024-09-28T13:44:29-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Vote - AcceptText - Agreed with all, though I would prefer discussion of the new reading ἐγκέκλικα. As for l. 25, it's unfortunate that the ed. pr.'s reg doesn't display, as it would make it clearer what the intervention is. I don't quite get Mike's point about the alt tag and hearing it either way. I find the new interpretation and punctuation convincing. </change>
          <change when="2024-01-12T11:22:56-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Mike%20Sampson">Vote - AcceptText - I agree with all proposals, but would prefer that the suggested rendering in line 25 be encoded using |alt| tags, since it could be heard either way. Finalizer, please also dot the first kappa of line 6 and add word-wrap line break to |reg| tags for ll. 5-6. Indent also line 26.</change>
          <change when="2024-01-02T05:52:09-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Corrections in three lines.</change>
          <change when="2024-01-02T05:51:28-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - A couple of corrections here. In l. 1 the iota adscript is used only in ἀδελφῶι. In ll. 5-6 I read ἐγκέκλικα (l. ἐγκέκλεικα), which is more meaningful. In l. 25, the regularization to an alleged infinitive στραγεῦσαι is unnecessary, the Aor. Subj is ok. A full stop after ἵνʼ εἰδῇς suffices to clarify the syntax (Therefore, I write to you so you know. Do not procrastinate). The text probably requires further changes as there are several issues to be addressed.</change>
